# D-MOUNT-RUNS-THE-ORPHAN-SWEEP-TWICE-BACK-TO-BACK: same-build A/B of
# orphan_sweep_coalesce (dlm/v5_mount.c v5_orphan_sweep_queue), run from
# ~/src/mxfs-e (srcversion 737E182A809291DAA0B4785, which carries the
# coalescing at its default 1) on 4/net/mesh/direct g4: the two-node TCP
# configurations are held by the H-F11 A/B, and the departure worker's queue
# is the same code on any TCP configuration.  One lap, four lone remounts of
# test3 after it unmounts as the last member, the knob alternating 0,1,0,1 on
# the same mount history (tests/orphan_sweep_coalesce_ab.sh, its header
# describes the shape).
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap; the harness applies them):
#   CONTROL (knob 0) REPRODUCED  every remount with a settled predecessor
#                                (P-SETTLED-INCARNATION) logs two
#                                P-DEPART-WORK-ORPHAN-SWEEP and no
#                                P-ORPHAN-SWEEP-COALESCED.
#   FIX (knob 1) PASS            every such remount logs one sweep, at least
#                                one COALESCED line, and its sweep's start
#                                (line time minus total_ms) is at or after the
#                                departure's completion line.
#   VACUOUS                      no remount met a settled predecessor.
#   FAIL                         any mount or unmount nonzero or over its
#                                bound, or a fix remount outside the rule.
#   FIXED AND VERIFIED needs the control arm REPRODUCED and every fix remount
#   PASS in the same lap.  A second lap on 2/net/mesh/direct, the
#   configuration the record was observed on, follows when that configuration
#   is free.
#
# Bound: the harness header's per-step bounds for NFILES=2000, CYCLES=4, four
# nodes: prep 300 + creates 140 + three departing unmounts 3x120 + four cycles
# x (last-member unmount 180 + knob 20 + mark 20 + lone mount 180 + quiet wait
# 2000x6/100+10+60 = 190 + line read 20 = 610) = 3240 s.
#
# osc4a (2026-10-17T19:20Z) measured nothing: the harness's quiet wait counted
# only P-DEPART-WORK lines, so it ended 10 s after 'P-DEPART-WORKER started'
# while the takeover was still retiring pages (708/646/585 P-TAUTH-TAKEOVER-
# RETIRE lines at the cut in cycles 1-3), and each next unmount cut that
# takeover and its sweep short; cycle 4's one sweep was still retiring cycle
# 1's leftover pages (via=orphan-sweep) when it was read.  The wait now counts
# every worker line and ends only after the departure line and a sweep line.
#
# osc4b (19:30Z) ran the shape in every cycle (sweeps visible) and graded
# FAIL on two harness checks, not on the behaviour: cycle 1 met TWO settled
# departures and swept three times (the mount's sweep plus one per departure),
# which the CONTROL rule above, written for one departure, read as not two;
# and both fix remounts (1 sweep, 1 COALESCED) computed their sweep's start
# 0.52 / 0.18 ms before the departure line it follows on the same worker,
# because total_ms is whole milliseconds and the start was rounded to 3
# decimals.  RULES AMENDED BEFORE osc4c (the next lap), stated in the
# behaviour's own terms: CONTROL REPRODUCED = sweeps equal the settled
# departures plus one, no COALESCED; FIX PASS = one sweep, at least one
# COALESCED, its start at or after the departure line within total_ms's 1 ms
# resolution.
#
# osc4c (19:36Z, 4/net/mesh/direct g4) PASS: control cycles 1 and 3 swept 4
# and 2 times after 3 and 1 settled departures, no COALESCED; fix cycles 2 and
# 4 swept once each, one COALESCED each, start after the departure line; every
# mount and unmount rc=0 (mounts 0.5-1.0 s, unmounts 1.0-4.2 s).  Next: the
# same lap on 2/net/mesh/direct g2c, the configuration the record was observed
# on.  Bound for two nodes: prep 300 + creates 140 + one departing unmount 120
# + four cycles x 610 = 3000 s.
3000 NFILES=2000 CYCLES=4 QUIET_S=10 tests/orphan_sweep_coalesce_ab.sh osc2a 2/net/mesh/direct g2c
